{
 "issue": 49,
 "title": "Noisy newest Dst hour copies with a dst_newest_unsettled flag feature, XGBoost, 1 hour",
 "result": "worse",
 "result_note": "label by the retrain policy bar, which is defined on clean validation: with flag 0 the flagged model (nf1) has 2.03% more overall MSE than the production configuration, interval [1.33, 2.67] above zero, so it is significantly worse and fails the issue's own 2% clean cost rule. The flag cuts the #30 V2 clean cost from +11.15% to +2.03% and on the perturbed copy with flag 1 it is 3.00% [-3.50, -2.51] below V2 K=1 overall (quiet RMSE 3.4352 nT against 3.4973 nT, below persistence from the perturbed Dst(t), 5.9748 nT). In storm hours of the perturbed copy flag 1 is worse than V2 K=1 (+6.29% [2.82, 12.12]) and not different from production (+3.89% [-8.69, 22.77]). The policy has no bar for the perturbed set; that decision stays with the owner.",
 "date": "2026-11-28",
 "split": "validation only, 2017-01-01 .. 2020-12-31; train 1995 .. 2016; the table was cut after 2021-01-01 00:00, which is used only as the target of the last validation hour, so no test row existed in the run (fit(..., test=False) as well)",
 "horizon_hours": 1,
 "configuration": {
  "baseline": "production configuration of scripts/train_xgb.py (6 lags, PARAMS, 89 features), seeds 0 1 2; seed 0 reproduces best_iteration 2151 and validation RMSE 2.6565 of reports/xgb_baseline.json",
  "v2k1": "scripts/train_xgb.py --dst-newest-noise 1 (issue 30 V2 K=1), rerun here as the reference for the flag; seeds 0 1 2 reproduce the best iterations and seed mean RMSE of reports/experiments/30-newest-dst-hour.json",
  "nf1": "scripts/train_xgb.py --dst-newest-flag 1: the same clean train years plus the same noisy copy as v2k1 (oculstorm.augment.newest_hour_error, level 1, seed 1), with the extra feature dst_newest_unsettled (build_features(newest_flag=...)), 0 on every clean row and 1 on the noisy copy; 90 features; seeds 0 1 2",
  "nf2": "--dst-newest-flag 2: as nf1 plus the half level copy of #30 (seed 2) with flag 0.5, to test the flag as a noise level",
  "early_stopping": "on the clean validation years with flag 0 for every variant, as in production",
  "perturbed_validation": "validation features rebuilt with the #30 recipe at full level and seed 12345 on the newest hour of every row, target clean; realised error in perturbation_on_validation (identical to #30). Scored with flag 1 (what live would set) and with flag 0 (to show what the flag buys). baseline and v2k1 have no flag column.",
  "references": "persistence from the clean Dst(t) and from the perturbed Dst(t)",
  "regimes": "by the clean observed Dst at the target hour",
  "not_run": "GRU: scripts/train_gru.py has no validation only mode, as in #30. Live use of the flag (oculstorm/live.py) is a follow up the issue leaves out.",
  "defaults": "--dst-newest-flag is 0 by default and build_features(newest_flag=None) adds no column; production features and results are unchanged. Refused together with --dst-newest-noise, --dst-skip, --ring-current and --dst-offset-aug."
